merko refers to the United States, much to the objection of Jorge.  One bit
of malglico of the merko variety is that I/we did not know at the time we
made the gismu that some languages usedthe word American to refer to the
combined North/South American unit as a single continent.  We have bemro and
ketco for North and South American respectively and xispo for Spanish-speaking
America (not quite identical to Latin America, which includes Brazil and
Belize which speak Portuguese and I think English).

